The 'unperturbed dimension' of the polymer chain is represented as,

(𝑟𝑜2 ̅̅̅)^{1/2} ∝𝑙̅(𝑛)^{1/2}

where,

(𝑟𝑜2 ̅̅̅)^{1/2}_{= root-mean square end-to-end distance} 𝑙̅ _{= average length of a segment}

𝑛 = number of segments in the chain

Using the above information, root-mean square end-to-end distance of a branched polyethylene would be _________________ when compared with that of the linear polyethylene of the same molecular weight and the same number of segments.

